;; Two arms of one `match` that give two different variants the same integer: `E::A => 2`,
;; `E::B => 2`.
;;
;; A hand-written codec's encoder (crates/hir-ty/src/mir/persist.rs) and identity.rs's
;; `request_index` give each variant its tag by hand; rustc reports a repeated pattern but not
;; a repeated result, so two variants on one tag encode to the same bytes and decode as one.
;; agents/annoyances/image-part-array-positional-callers.json: `Part::DefMap` held tag 2, the
;; next free part's. Variants are told apart by what their paths resolve to; an or-pattern
;; (`A | B => 1`) is one arm and says the sharing on purpose.
;;
;; Rule 73: a type ends it (tags derived from the declaration, or `#[repr(u8)]` discriminants,
;; which rustc keeps unique); `hand_written_codec` reads fields, not tags. Rule meanwhile.

(include "tools/astlog/rules-sema/lib/int-arms.astlog")

;; A later arm `b` of the same match counts another variant as the same integer.
(rule (tag-collision b i a)
  (indexed m a i d)
  (indexed m b i e)
  (precedes a b)
  (not (indexed m b i d)))

(lint tag-collision error "this arm's tag $i is already an earlier arm's, for another variant")
